<title>UK: GA, CU up amid renewed bid talk.</title>
<headline>GA, CU up amid renewed bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in General Accident Plc and Commercial Union Plc were among the biggest gainers in the UK market on Thursday, caught up in the latest wave of bid speculation in the insurance sector, analysts and dealers said.</p>
<p>GA was up 23p or 2.9 percent at 820, while CU was up 24-1/2p or 3.5 percent at 719-1/2. Traders said bid hopes had resurfaced following Prudential Corp Plc's 1.9 billion stg bid for mutually-owned Scottish Amicable.</p>
<p>&quot;The sector is full of takeover froth,&quot; said one insurance analyst.</p>
</text>
